{"agent":"exp5-rules","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The stated intent is \"decisions in force (accepted/proposed, not superseded)\", but `_decisions` only rejects `d.status == \"superseded\"` (or a set `superseded_by`) and never checks that the status is one of the in-force statuses. Any decision carrying a non-in-force status that is not literally \"superseded\" flows through. For example, given a decision with `status=\"rejected\"` (or `\"deprecated\"`/`\"withdrawn\"`), `d.superseded_by` empty and a governing glob, the loop at lines 48–51 does not `continue`; the row is built and appended to `by_glob`/`loose`, and it is then counted by `decision_count` and exported as binding. The result is a RULES.md that presents a rejected decision as in force, contradicting the documented \"accepted/proposed\" definition and the acceptance criterion that only in-force decisions appear. The fix is to skip `d.status not in (\"accepted\", \"proposed\")` before building the row.","digest":"9413f355e1f5dd54","location":"ddflow/services/export/kind_rules.py:49 (`_decisions` status filter)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/export/kind_rules.py:49 (`_decisions` status filter)"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":17469,"diff_sha":"3681d0f84680e237359a23ce4ff527c3c767ec4d80d6f552d8dfe34e597f0951","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-export-rules","elapsed_s":691.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/services/export/kind_rules.py:49 (`_decisions` status filter)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e898cac84cce6cea2ace2b07f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10208,"schema":1,"subject":"B-export-rules","ts