{"agent":"exp5-rules","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":4,"detail":"The test renders `_body(q, tag=\"storage\")` and asserts `\"`D-free`\" not in t`, i.e. it expects the `tag` filter to remove a decision that has no tags. The stated intent is that decisions are selected and grouped by governing path, while `--tag` is described as a lesson filter (“lessons are summarised, with a --limit and --tag filter”). In the fixture `D-free` is an accepted decision with no governing path, so a tag-filtered RULES.md should still contain it under “No governing path”. This assertion instead enshrines a behaviour where filtering by a lesson tag silently drops decisions in force; an implementation that correctly filters only lessons by tag would fail this test.","digest":"feca374984ca5ce8","location":"tests/test_export_rules.py:test_tag_filter_and_limit","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_export_rules.py:test_tag_filter_and_limit"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":19945,"diff_sha":"337817a5ddc47ca9afd3685b7049fe3985031eeafbfdcd5e877a9767018f2836","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-export-rules","elapsed_s":588.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_export_rules.py:test_tag_filter_and_limit"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"efca93f9a6aacd0659624fddb","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":10328,"schema":1,"subject":"B-export-rules","ts":"2026-10-02T14:36:07.907242Z"}
